&lt;h1&gt;Site Reliability Engineer (Apprentice) - France&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Horizon Trading Solutions ?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Une Fintech spécialisée dans la conception d’une plateforme facilitant les différentes activités de trading sur les marchés financiers électroniques (automatisation de certaines activités (Market Making, Algo Trading...), gestion des ordres et exécutions de manière optimale (Agency Trading, Order and Execution Management System…) ,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Un logiciel à la fine pointe de la technologie déployée sur site ou en Managed Services ,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Une roadmap produit ambitieuse : Machine Learning, IA, Crypto Currencies, Low Latency…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Une société à taille humaine (1 20 collaborateurs) où vous pouvez faire une différence ,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Une société internationale présente dans 6 pays pour servir des clients répartis sur 26 pays ,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Une société engagée : certifié B-Corp, partenaire de Planet Tech’care, Ethical IA et Lakaa , fond de dotation ,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Une société reconnue dans son domaine : Best Sell Side OMS 2025, Best Multi-Asset Trading System 2025, Best trading solution for listed securities 2022 et 2023...&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Ce que vous ferez chez nous (Spoiler : c&#39;est passionnant techniquement !)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Concevoir et mettre en œuvre une infrastructure performante et évolutive :&lt;/strong&gt; participez à la création et au déploiement d&#39;infrastructures critiques pour notre offre de services managés, intégrant hébergement, connectivité aux échanges et gestion des données de marché.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Déployer des solutions robustes et optimisées :&lt;/strong&gt; travaillez sur des environnements variés (on-premises, colocation, cloud) dans une infrastructure distribuée mondiale, répondant aux exigences de performances élevées et de latence minimale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Moderniser notre écosystème technologique :&lt;/strong&gt; migrez des services existants vers une architecture basée sur des microservices et des conteneurs (Docker, Kubernetes), tout en améliorant notre pile de déploiement et d&#39;intégration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Garantir la fiabilité des plateformes :&lt;/strong&gt; automatisez les tâches de maintenance, mettez en place un monitoring en temps réel, effectuez des vérifications proactives et assurez les mises à jour et correctifs nécessaires.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Renforcer la sécurité de nos systèmes :&lt;/strong&gt; déployez des solutions innovantes pour protéger nos plateformes hébergées et assurez leur conformité aux standards de sécurité, SOC2 notamment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Veiller au respect des processus :&lt;/strong&gt; appliquez rigoureusement les procédures de gestion des changements (CAB, &quot;validation à 4 yeux&quot;, gestion d&#39;accès temporaire).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partager et promouvoir les meilleures pratiques :&lt;/strong&gt; participez activement à la sensibilisation technologique, à la normalisation des outils et méthodes, et collaborez avec des experts dans un environnement Agile et DevOps.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborer dans un cadre international :&lt;/strong&gt; échangez avec des équipes réparties dans plusieurs fuseaux horaires et intervenez sur des projets mondiaux impliquant Horizon, ses clients et partenaires.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Vos indispensables :&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La volonté de travailler du dimanche au vendredi inclus afin d’assurer une couverture optimale pour nos clients ,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Administration des systèmes Linux (RHEL) et scripting (bash, python, Gitlab , Ansible ).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Développement Python&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Configuration CI-CD et outils associés (e.g. Gitlab CI, ArgoCD ou équivalent)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Déploiements et configuration Docker ou Kubernetes&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Utilisation d’une solution de monitoring (idéalement Datadog ou équivalent )&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Première expérience avec un fournisseur de services Cloud ( idéalement Azure)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connaissances en:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Architectures On prem et Cloud&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Réseau : VLAN, routage IP, BGP, pare-feu (VPN, règles)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Systèmes d&#39;alerting et procédures&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Méthodologies Agile et DevOps&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Vos super-pouvoirs (si vous les avez, on adore encore plus) :&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compétences en réseau : VLAN, routage IP, pare-feu (VPN, règles)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Expérience avec infrastructure-as-code (e.g. Terraform , Cloud init )&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bonnes bases en déploiement ou développement d&#39;applications Python ( Django) ou Java (Spring, Quark us)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Administration des bases de données PostgreSQL&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Expérience avec Prometheus, InfluxDB, Telegraf ou Grafana&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Expérience dans un modèle de travail &quot;follow the sun&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connaissances des opérations d&#39;applications de trading ou financières&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connaissances d ’un ou plusieurs référentiel (s) de sécurité et de processus d’audit type SOC2&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La maîtrise d e l’angla is écrit et parlé est un atout&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Pourquoi nous rejoindre ?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexibilité et équilibre :&lt;/strong&gt; télétravail jusqu’à 1 jour par semaine&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Réalisez vos rêves tech :&lt;/strong&gt; Machine Learning, IA, crypto, microservices, ultra-low latency... Chez nous, vous pouvez les explorer à fond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Impact immédiat :&lt;/strong&gt; travaillez sur des solutions critiques utilisées dans le monde entier.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grandissez avec nous :&lt;/strong&gt; projets stimulants et experts passionnés à vos côtés.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rémunération : &lt;/strong&gt;La rémunération et les avantages sont déterminés conformément à notre politique de rémunération et aux dispositions de la convention collective Syntec.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alors n’hésitez pas et rejoignez l’aventure Horizon !&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Horizon is an equal opportunity employer. We promote diversity, multiculturalism, and inclusion.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Winton&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Winton is a research-based investment management company with a specialist focus on statistical and mathematical inference in financial markets. The firm researches and trades quantitative investment strategies, which are implemented systematically via thousands of securities, spanning the world&#39;s major liquid asset classes. Founded in 1997 by David Harding, Winton today manages assets for some of the world’s largest institutional investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We employ ambitious professionals who want to work collaboratively at the leading edge of investment management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek a highly skilled developer with strong computer science fundamentals to join our Quantitative Platform team. This team is responsible for developing the core platforms that underpin and provide data to the research and trading of our quantitative investment strategies, alongside tools, APIs, libraries, and user interfaces to support this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will work closely with our research and other technology teams to deliver high impact projects that improve our ability to predict and trade movements in global financial markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Technology&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating in a cloud-first environment, we predominantly write our backend systems in C# but otherwise make pragmatic choices for each scenario. This often means Python with C++ employed in performance-sensitive cases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our applications are written with containerisation in mind from the outset and deployed as a Docker image into Kubernetes on AWS where we can scale on-demand to satisfy burstable workloads. We make extensive use of Kafka for low-latency communication across applications and use a mixture of different technologies for storage, from S3 to relational databases. We utilise GitHub for source control and Jenkins for CI, though with an increasing interest in GitHub Actions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We constantly evaluate our stack to ensure we’re using the most appropriate technologies for the needs of our business and the efficient delivery of those requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a world-class platform that enables storage, transformation, and testing of data at scale by leveraging the latest open-source software, cloud, and distributed computing technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain a deep understanding of the requirements of our research teams to deliver business-critical functionality in a timely-manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the team through active contribution in code reviews, knowledge-sharing, and design discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and maintain good quality, well-tested code across services, data storage and UI layers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Bachelors or Masters degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, Statistics, Physics or equivalent technical field.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of professional software development experience, including C#, Python or C++&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using agentic AI coding tools such as Claude Code and are genuinely keen to use them as a natural part of daily work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative nature and ability to work in a team e.g., partnering with portfolio managers, quantitative researchers, and other technologists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in keeping abreast of latest technologies and a measured approach for adopting them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with problem solving across multiple technologies and business domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What would Be Useful:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engineering systems for the cloud-based storage and processing of large datasets or using frameworks such as Spark and open standards like Parquet and Arrow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with other cloud and related technologies, such as Docker and Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working as a software developer in the quantitative hedge fund space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Experience building web applications using front-end frameworks such as Angular.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Equal Opportunity Workplace&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or any other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Cato Networks is the converged network and security cloud for the AI era.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;As AI reshapes cybersecurity, enterprises face a dual challenge: unlocking AI’s potential while defending against AI-driven attacks. Cato addresses both through a unified, cloud-native platform, providing the visibility and context to prioritize risks and stop threats in real time across users, applications, data, and AI agents.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Join us as we scale: take on ambitious technological challenges and shape the next generation of enterprise security at a company trusted by thousands of organizations worldwide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559737&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:225,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:279}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As a Cato AI Security &lt;strong&gt;Professional Services Consultant&lt;/strong&gt;, you will be a trusted advisor to our customers to help see them through their AI security implementation journey. You will provide technical guidance and direction to ensure the Cato AI security solution&#39;s smooth and successful implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Curiosity&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; – You have a desire to truly understand our customers&#39; business needs.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Creativity&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; – You can find a sustainable path to yes.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Empathy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; – You connect at a human level with our customers, and you genuinely care&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain expert-level implementation proficiency of the Cato Networks AI Security solution while keeping abreast of the dynamic AI security and enterprise IT infrastructure landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop meaningful relationships with key customer stakeholders and their partners, adopting a consultative and prescriptive approach that inspires trust and confidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end customer engagements implementing Cato AI security solution for AI risk management, model security, and data protection so that our customers can realize the total value of their investment in our technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with customer teams to design secure AI architectures and establish governance frameworks aligned to standards such as NIST AI RMF, ISO/IEC 42001, and EU AI Act guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate technical findings into actionable recommendations for both executive and technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a subject matter expert on AI and LLM security across the Cato Networks customer base&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to development of internal knowledge sharing, solution playbooks, and enablement materials for partners and customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster collaboration with our product management, support and engineering teams by providing feedback from the field on features and functionality, influencing roadmap priorities based on customer needs and emerging threats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support pre-sales scoping of professional services for new customer engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to expand customer value through additional AI security services and capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration with greater professional services team to help synthesize experiences and trends observed in the field into repeatable technical best practices in collaboration with other Cato functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate day-to-day with minimal oversite as a point of technical escalation to provide guidance on and ensure timely resolution of any issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in cloud architecture with a primary focus on AWS or Azure, including hands-on deployment and management of Amazon EKS or ECS, or Azure Kubernetes Service and hybrid connectivity services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in a customer-facing role (e.g., consulting, professional services, pre-sales, managed services) for a high-tech software or technology vendor with a proven track record leading enterprise consulting or professional services engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to implementation of API gateways (e.g., Zuul, Apigee, Kong, Amazon API Gateway, Azure API Management) and AI application specific gateways (e.g., LiteLLM, Portkey, Helicone, TrueFoundry)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of public cloud networking constructs (e.g., AWS VPCs, Transit Gateway, Direct Connect, Route 53, and Gateway Load Balancer – Azure VNets, VNGs, ExpressRoute, vWAN, Load Balancer, and DNS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and securing AI/ML infrastructure including AWS SageMaker, AWS Bedrock, Azure AI Foundry, Google Vertex AI, Databricks, GPU-accelerated compute, and model inference pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to unique threat landscape for AI and LLMs including AI specific threat models and risks (e.g., prompt injection, data poisoning/leakage/exfiltration, model inversion/manipulations/poisoning, and other adversarial attacks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with Infrastructure as Code (IaC) using Terraform, CloudFormation, or CDK with version-controlled deployment pipelines and automation scripting skills in Python, Bash, or Go is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with container security, runtime protection, and service mesh architectures (Istio, App Mesh)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with observability and monitoring stacks (e.g., CloudWatch, Prometheus, Grafana, Datadog)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of data sovereignty, residency requirements and compliance frameworks relevant to AI workloads (e.g., FedRAMP, SOC 2, ISO 27001, NIST 800-53, HIPPA, PCI, HITRUST, GDPR)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data protection regulations and AI Security frameworks (e.g., GDPR, NIST AI RMF, ISO/IEC 27001, ISO/IEC 42001, OWASP Top 10 for LLMs, MITRE ATLAS) is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, capable of influencing at all levels and gaining a ‘Trusted Advisor’ status with key stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry accredited security certifications (e.g., CISSP, CCSK, CISM) and AI security–specific credentials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent troubleshooting and problem-solving skills with an innate ability to methodically get to the root of issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very well organized and work effectively in an agile and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid command of the English language (written and spoken) with additional language skills is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working within a geographically distributed and diverse team for a hypergrowth global organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 25% of the time for customer on-site meetings and various company meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About CoLab&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoLab, we help mechanical engineering teams bring life-changing products to market years sooner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build AI for engineers designing cars, medical devices, and jet engines. Products this complex aren&#39;t sketched and sent to production. Teams spend months on iterations, reviews, and tests, predicting how every part performs before anything is built. CoLab is where those reviews happen, and we capture the rationale behind every change. Other tools show what changed between versions. Only CoLab knows why. That&#39;s how our AI helps manufacturers like Bobcat, Triumph Motorcycles, and GE Appliances make better decisions, eliminate rework cycles, and get to market faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proudly based in St. John’s, Newfoundland, CoLab started with one customer in 2018. Since then we’ve raised a&lt;a href=&quot;https://financialpost.com/pmn/business-wire-news-releases-pmn/ai-is-changing-engineering-colab-just-raised-72m-to-lead-the-transformation&quot;&gt; $72M Series C&lt;/a&gt;, been named the 57th fastest growing company in North America by Deloitte (&lt;a href=&quot;https://financialpost.com/pmn/business-wire-news-releases-pmn/colab-ranked-number-57-fastest-growing-company-in-north-america-on-the-2025-deloitte-technology-fast-500&quot;&gt;Fast 500™&lt;/a&gt;), signed multi-year&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/article-bombardier-signs-contract-colab-ai-software/&quot;&gt; AI partnerships with companies like Bombardier&lt;/a&gt;, and grown to a team of 250+.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact role that helps define how CoLab delivers technical value to its most strategic customers in Aerospace and Defence. CoLab is a category-creating product, which means adoption isn&#39;t just a rollout. It&#39;s a change in how the organization works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;d act as a trusted advisor, leveraging people, process, and technology to help teams rethink how they manage feedback, data, and decision-making across design and PLM. That means getting deep into customer workflows, testing new ways of working, and building repeatable methods the rest of the team can scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work alongside a Customer Success Manager, and use what you learn on the front line to help shape product direction. This role isn&#39;t about selling or pitching. It&#39;s about deeply understanding engineering problems and solving them alongside the customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a candidate in Switzerland to work regularly on-site with local CoLab customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Ideal Candidate&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re a mechanical engineer by trade and have worked as a designer in an A&amp;amp;D company. You also understand the full product development life cycle: how design, manufacturing, quality, and engineering leadership depend on each other, and where collaboration breaks down. You can coach those teams toward working together better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You know how to improve that life cycle with technology. Maybe you’ve championed internal tools or created automation or scripts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You also know a process that makes sense on paper won’t get adopted on its own. You can meet people where they are, including the stakeholders who don’t want to change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don’t need to be the loudest voice in the room, but you can run a sprint and lead a cross-functional project. If the average person might find this job too undefined or complex, that probably excites you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Job Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mapping a customer&#39;s current-state design review and engineering workflows, and defining the target-state process their teams will actually adopt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploying and tuning CoLab&#39;s AI capabilities against a customer&#39;s own standards, drawing checklists, and design guidelines, and diagnosing what&#39;s working and what isn&#39;t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing mechanical engineering expertise to validate AI-generated results and ensure engineering rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigating and solving complex engineering data and integration challenges across PLM, ERP, QMS, and traditional design feedback tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expanding adoption into new teams, programs, and sites within the account, partnering with the Customer Success Manager on where the next opportunity sits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with product teams to identify feature gaps, improve capabilities, and refine AutoReview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in mechanical design engineering, ideally in a medium- to large-sized organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of PLM &amp;amp; ERP systems and enterprise engineering data architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead technical projects and cross-functional collaborations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with customers or internal stakeholders to solve technical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in fast-changing, ambiguous environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication and documentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of high-level AI architecture, specifically LLMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with APIs, data integrations, and enterprise architecture concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Located in Switzerland&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with internal tool development, scripting, or automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to AI/ML tools applied to engineering workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work in design consulting or product development at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While this is a fully remote role, travel is a consistent part of the job. There are two primary types of travel you can expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Weeks:&lt;/strong&gt; Once per quarter, the sales team or entire company gets together in person. These typically involve traveling out on a Monday and returning on a Thursday or Friday. Two of these each year are held at our headquarters in St. John&#39;s, Newfoundland, Canada and the others take place in more central locations that evolve as the team grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-sites:&lt;/strong&gt; This role will work closely with a local customer with expectations to be on site with that customer, so there will likely be far less travel than our typical MFDE roll. That being said, in the event the local customer were to no longer work with us, the following is our standard MFDE travel expectations: “For most of our large deployment customers, we will visit on-site during kick-off and key expansion opportunities. Most on-sites involve 2-3 days with the customer, with travel on either side. Travel is primarily within North America, and you can expect 4 customer on-sites per quarter.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Extra Details&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a full-time, permanent position with a competitive compensation package that includes stock options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited paid vacation and extended health benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Equity Note&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Frequently cited statistics show that people who identify with historically marginalized groups are likely to apply to jobs only if they meet 100% of the qualifications. We encourage you to help us break that statistic and apply even if you don&#39;t meet every single qualification. Your potential is what matters most to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;About us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coalition is the world&#39;s first Active Insurance provider designed to help prevent digital risk before it strikes. Founded in 2017, Coalition combines comprehensive insurance coverage and innovative cybersecurity tools to help businesses manage and mitigate potential cyberattacks.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Opportunities to make an impact with bold thinking are real—and happening daily at Coalition.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Major Account Executive to own and grow a book of strategic enterprise accounts. This is a role for someone who can run complex, multi-threaded sales cycles into security-conscious buying committees (CISO, CIO, procurement, legal, and often the board) and close 3-year enterprise commitments in a competitive, incumbent-heavy market, while navigating channel partners (e.g. VARs and Distributors).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be selling into organizations where a security failure is existential, where the buying process is genuinely adversarial by design, and where trust is earned through technical credibility and long-term relationships, not charisma. If you&#39;ve sold into security teams before, you know this isn&#39;t a &quot;build rapport and close&quot; motion — it&#39;s proving you understand the threat model as well as the buyer does.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and grow a book of major/strategic accounts, running the full cycle from qualification through multi-year contract negotiation and close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate multi-stakeholder buying committees — security, IT, legal, procurement, and executive sponsors — building consensus across functions with genuinely competing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with technical presales Solutions Architects to run live technical evaluations and proof-of-concepts that hold up under real scrutiny from technical buyers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure and negotiate enterprise contracts, with a strong bias toward multi-year (3-year) terms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and defend a business case that speaks fluently to both risk reduction (CISO language) and ROI (CFO language) — you need both, not one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate forecasting and pipeline hygiene on long-cycle (6–9 month), high-ACV deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize Customer Success for account health, since renewal risk on an account this size is a shared problem, not a handoff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Skills and Qualifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8+ years of closing experience in enterprise cybersecurity/SaaS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to close deals upwards of $1M ARR or more and 6+ month sales cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of navigating security-specific procurement: vendor risk assessments, SOC 2 / ISO 27001 diligence, security questionnaires, and legal review cycles that are more adversarial than typical SaaS procurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort being technically challenged in a room — you don&#39;t need to be an engineer, but you need to hold your own when a CISO pressure-tests your claims&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience structuring and closing multi-year contracts, not just annual renewals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hunter mentality — use relationships &amp;amp; partnerships to find leverage to close deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;and this role rewards depth and judgment over sheer volume&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Perks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;p-rich_text_list p-rich_text_list__bullet&quot; data-stringify-type=&quot;unordered-list&quot; data-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% medical coverage, including outpatient care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25+ paid holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual home office stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7% employer pension contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental and physical health wellness programs like Headspace, Wellhub&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation and opportunity for advancement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Why Coalition?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work at Coalition is centered on the joint mission to Protect the Unprotected. We have built a remote-first, highly inclusive culture that welcomes people from diverse backgrounds. We trust each other to take responsibility, share ownership of outcomes, and put in the work together to protect businesses from digital risk. Coalition’s exceptional growth stems from its ability to address real-world problems for organizations of all sizes while remaining true to our founding values of character, humility, responsibility, purpose, authenticity, and inclusion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re always looking for collaborative, inquisitive individuals to join #OurCoalition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.coalitioninc.com/newsroom&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Visit our Newsroom &amp;gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coalition is committed to protecting your privacy and handling your personal information responsibly. We collect, use, and store personal information as necessary for the recruitment process and in compliance with applicable privacy laws and regulations in all regions where we operate. We want you to understand what personal information we collect, how we use it, and your rights regarding access, correction, and deletion of your data where applicable. Information submitted, collected, and processed as part of your application is subject to Coalition&#39;s Privacy Policy. For further details, please review our full Privacy Policy or contact us with any questions regarding how your information is handled.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.coalitioninc.com/legal/privacy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Our Privacy Policy &amp;gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
